fragment-sort

Generate a priority list for mksquashfs by grouping files and file tails
with similar contents. The prebuilt x86-64 executable uses the build host's
Zstandard and C++ runtime libraries (libzstd1 and libstdc++6 on Debian).
Slax includes both in 01-core.sb.

From this directory, with the original filesystem mounted at /mnt/source:

    chmod +x fragment-sort
    ./fragment-sort /mnt/source -b 1M -tailends --zstd-score --candidates 16 -o core.sort

Pass -sort core.sort -b 1M -tailends -action 'fragment(mixed)@true' to
mksquashfs. Keep the sort list and output image outside the source tree.

To rebuild the dynamically linked executable on Slax or Debian,
install the build dependencies as root.

    apt install g++ libzstd-dev

From this directory, compile and strip the executable in one command.

    g++ -std=c++17 -O2 -s -D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64 -DZSTD_SUPPORT \
        fragment-sort.cpp fragment-order.cpp fragment-score.cpp -o fragment-sort -lzstd
